From 026ed78966262de11ab6877776b265526b2adb7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 01:20:13 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fall back to a private reader when the shared cached_ro
 reader is borrowed

Concurrent dashboard readers on hermes-hub (session-panel feed, /session-cards,
sidebar) collided on the one shared read-only connection per board and raised
"database is locked: cached reader is borrowed" (165 times in one errors.log),
flipping Desktop status panels to unknown.

cached_ro now waits at most 50 ms (or the remaining budget) for the shared
connection, then opens a private read-only connection with the same opener and
the rest of the budget as its busy timeout, yields it and always closes it. The
shared cache entry is untouched by the fallback. borrow_lock keeps its raising
contract on top of a new try_borrow helper. ro_stats["private_fallbacks"]
counts fallbacks so live contention is visible.

replica_task_resolution moves unchanged to
kanban_session_activity_replica_resolution.py (re-exported) to keep
kanban_session_activity.py under its 2000-line health cap.

Co-Authored-By: Contributor <contributor@example.com>
